course: dictionary
lesson: 11909
title: Buoyant: floating, cheerful, or doing well
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Use the words around it to find the right one. «The buoyant boat bobbed on the waves.» Bobbed on the waves tells you the boat floats, so buoyant means able to float.
explain: Feelings can be buoyant too. «Mia felt buoyant after the good news, and she skipped all the way home.» Skipping shows a happy, hopeful mood, so buoyant means cheerful and full of hope.
explain: Money can be buoyant as well. «Sales were buoyant all summer, so the shop hired two new workers.» Hiring more workers suggests business is doing well. Swap in your meaning to check it still makes sense.
fact: «Buoyant» means able to float, or able to keep things floating.
fact: «Buoyant» can also mean cheerful and full of hope.
fact: A buoyant market or economy is one where prices or sales are rising.
fact: In science, the water pushes up on a floating object (upthrust) as much as its weight pushes down.
fact: Salt water is more buoyant than fresh water, so swimmers float more easily in the sea.
exercise: «The buoyant boat bobbed on the waves, light and steady.» What does buoyant mean here? | Old and broken | Very heavy and slow | Painted in bright colours | *Able to float
exercise: «Mia felt buoyant after she heard the good news.» What does buoyant suggest? | Very hungry | Tired and cross | Wet and cold | *Cheerful and full of hope
exercise: «Salt water is more buoyant than fresh water, so swimmers float more easily in the sea.» Which is true? | *Salt water helps things float more | Fresh water helps things float more | Salt water makes everything sink | Buoyant means heavy
test: «The economy was buoyant, with shops selling more every month.» What does buoyant mean here? | Angry at the shopkeepers | Able to float | Empty and quiet | *Doing well, with sales rising
test: The armband is buoyant, so Sam stays up on the water. What does buoyant mean? | Very heavy | Quiet and still | *Able to float | Painted bright red
exam: Which sentence uses buoyant to mean cheerful? | *The buoyant puppy wagged its tail and bounced around the garden. | The buoyant market was closed on Sunday. | The buoyant stone sank to the bottom of the pond. | The buoyant ship was tied to the dock.
